---
description: Keep changes scoped and fast — match effort to the size of the request
alwaysApply: true
---

# Scope the work to what was asked

This is a UI prototype. Most requests are small, targeted edits to one section.
Treat them that way.

- Change only the section named. Don't refactor neighbours, rename things, or
  "improve" nearby code that wasn't mentioned.
- Don't add features, sections, or mock data that weren't asked for. If
  something adjacent looks wrong, mention it in one sentence instead of fixing it.
- Only plan out loud (todo lists, multi-step breakdowns) when the request really
  spans several files. A one-section change needs none of that.

# Match verification to the size of the change

The default is minimal. The user prefers to look at the result themselves.

For a small change — styling, wording, spacing, one component:

- Make the edit and report back. That's it.
- No production build, no headless browser screenshots, no clicking through
  unrelated tabs.

For a large change — a new page, many files, new data model:

- Type-check and check lints before reporting.
- Screenshot only if it genuinely helps show what changed.

# Never deploy unless asked

Do not build, commit, push, or deploy to Vercel on your own. Wait for the user to
say "upload", "live link", or similar. When they do ask, push and share
https://carrier-sourcing-web.vercel.app — and don't sit waiting on the deploy to
verify unless they ask you to confirm it.
